//@version=6
// ==============================================================================================
//                      M A R K E T   S E S S I O N S   O V E R V I E W   P A N E L
// ==============================================================================================
//
//  Indicator Name : Market Sessions Overview Panel
//  Author         : Forex_Market_Insights
//  Version        : v6.0 - July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Overlay indicator (plots on the price chart)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I am Forex_Market_Insights, the publisher and sole original author of this exact
//  implementation of "Market Sessions Overview Panel." I designed the architecture of this tool,
//  wrote every line of the Pine Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple
//  asset classes and timeframes, and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the per-session state machine that opens,
//  tracks and closes each session independently; the live open, high, low, close and activity
//  accumulator that updates on every bar inside a session; the range box construction with its
//  dashed boundary and per-session colouring; the optional session candle rendering that expresses
//  an entire session as a single body and wick; the automatic vertical label stagger that keeps
//  overlapping sessions readable; the change calculation in both absolute and percentage terms;
//  the text-rendered miniature candle used inside the summary panel; the live status model with
//  its open and closed indicators; the configurable summary panel with its ordering, positioning
//  and per-session colour treatment; the drawing history manager that retires the oldest sessions;
//  the timeframe suitability guard; the tooltip detail layer; and the alert framework.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.0, July 2026). Any future
//  modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  O R I G I N A L   I N D I C A T O R   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N
//  V E R I F I C A T I O N   A N D   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Forex_Market_Insights. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected or
//  open-source script. No third-party library and no republished open-source script forms any part
//  of this work, and no other author's visual system was reproduced.
//
//  I acknowledge openly that the underlying subject matter is entirely public. The existence and
//  the conventional clock times of the Tokyo, London, New York and Sydney trading sessions are
//  public market facts belonging to no author. The practice of shading a session on a chart, of
//  reading its open, high, low and close, and of noting that the London and New York overlap
//  carries the heaviest liquidity, is common knowledge taught freely across the trading community.
//
//  My original contribution, and what this declaration covers, is the specific code
//  implementation: my own per-session state machine, my own accumulator design, my own box and
//  session-candle construction, my own label stagger algorithm, my own text-rendered miniature
//  candle method, my own panel architecture and ordering model, my own history retirement logic,
//  and my own presentation layer. Conceptual overlap with other session tools is therefore
//  unavoidable and expected, since we are all displaying the same public market hours, but there
//  is no source-code overlap of any kind with any other author's work.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H A T   T H I S   I N D I C A T O R   D O E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Foreign exchange and metals trade around the clock, but they do not trade the same way around
//  the clock. Tokyo is typically quiet and range-bound. London brings the largest directional
//  moves. New York carries the data releases. The overlap between London and New York is the
//  deepest liquidity window of the day. A chart that does not show you which session produced a
//  move is hiding a large part of the explanation for that move.
//
//  This tool marks each session as it happens and reports exactly what it did.
//
//  1) SESSION TRACKING
//     Four sessions are defined with fully editable clock times and a selectable timezone. The
//     moment a session opens, the engine records its opening price and begins tracking its running
//     high, low, close and activity. Every bar inside the session updates those values live. When
//     the session closes, the values lock and the block becomes a permanent record.
//
//  2) RANGE BLOCKS
//     Each session is drawn as a dashed box spanning its exact time range and its full high to low
//     range, filled in that session's own colour. Where two sessions overlap, which happens by
//     design between London and New York, the two fills combine and the overlap is immediately
//     visible as a darker area. That overlap is the most important window on the chart.
//
//  3) SESSION CANDLES
//     Optionally, each session can additionally be expressed as a single candle: a body from its
//     open to its close and a wick spanning its full range. This compresses an entire eight-hour
//     session into one readable shape.
//
//  4) SESSION LABELS
//     Above each block, a label reports the session name, its closing price and its change in both
//     absolute and percentage terms. Because sessions overlap, labels are automatically staggered
//     vertically by session so they never collide.
//
//  5) LIVE SUMMARY PANEL
//     A panel reports every enabled session side by side: an open or closed status indicator, the
//     session name, its price, its percentage change, and a miniature candle rendered from that
//     session's own open, high, low and close so its character is readable at a glance. Position,
//     ordering and size are all configurable.
//
//  6) DETAIL TOOLTIPS
//     Hovering a session label or a panel cell reveals the full open, high, low, close, range and
//     accumulated activity for that session, so the extra detail is available without cluttering
//     the chart with it.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  T I M E F R A M E   A N D   M A R K E T   C O M P A T I B I L I T Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  The tool contains no price constants and no instrument-specific numbers. It reads only clock
//  time and the bar's own open, high, low and close, so it behaves identically on any instrument
//  that trades through the sessions being displayed: Forex majors and crosses, gold and other
//  metals, index CFDs, energies and crypto.
//
//  Sessions are a division of the trading day, so the tool is meaningful on intraday timeframes.
//  On daily and higher timeframes a single bar spans several sessions at once and the concept
//  breaks down. Rather than drawing something misleading, the script detects this and displays a
//  clear notice instead. The label stagger and the miniature candles scale from the instrument's
//  own range, so a chart priced at 0.65 and one priced at 4000 both render correctly.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  L I V E   B E H A V I O U R   A N D   R E P A I N T I N G   S T A T E M E N T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A session that has closed is final. Its box, its label, its values and its panel entry never
//  change afterwards.
//
//  The session currently in progress updates live on every tick, which is the entire point: its
//  box extends, its high and low widen, its close and change track the market, and its status
//  indicator shows it as open. When it closes, those values lock. This is correct live behaviour
//  rather than repainting, and no historical session is ever redrawn or moved.
//
//  No request.security call is used anywhere in this script, so there is no higher-timeframe
//  dependency and no lookahead risk of any kind.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S C L A I M E R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial
//  advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. Session behaviour
//  is a tendency and not a rule, and any session can behave completely out of character on any
//  given day. Use proper risk management and consult a licensed financial advisor before trading
//  real capital.
// ==============================================================================================

indicator("Market Sessions Overview Panel", "Sessions", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gGen = "=====  GENERAL  ====="
tz        = input.string("UTC", "Timezone", options = ["UTC", "Exchange", "America/New_York", "America/Chicago", "Europe/London", "Europe/Berlin", "Asia/Tokyo", "Asia/Shanghai", "Asia/Hong_Kong", "Asia/Dubai", "Asia/Karachi", "Asia/Kolkata", "Australia/Sydney"], group = gGen)
maxHist   = input.int(12, "Sessions Kept Per Market", minval = 1, maxval = 60, group = gGen, tooltip = "How many past sessions of each market stay drawn before the oldest is retired.")
tfGuard   = input.bool(true, "Warn On Unsuitable Timeframe", group = gGen, tooltip = "Sessions divide the trading day, so they are only meaningful intraday. On daily and higher this shows a notice instead of drawing something misleading.")

gTk = "=====  TOKYO  ====="
tkOn   = input.bool(true, "Enable", group = gTk, inline = "t")
tkSess = input.session("0000-0900", "", group = gTk, inline = "t")
tkCol  = input.color(#c14fd4, "", group = gTk, inline = "t")

gLd = "=====  LONDON  ====="
ldOn   = input.bool(true, "Enable", group = gLd, inline = "l")
ldSess = input.session("0700-1500", "", group = gLd, inline = "l")
ldCol  = input.color(#ff6b35, "", group = gLd, inline = "l")

gNy = "=====  NEW YORK  ====="
nyOn   = input.bool(true, "Enable", group = gNy, inline = "n")
nySess = input.session("1300-2000", "", group = gNy, inline = "n")
nyCol  = input.color(#26c6da, "", group = gNy, inline = "n")

gSy = "=====  SYDNEY  ====="
syOn   = input.bool(false, "Enable", group = gSy, inline = "s")
sySess = input.session("2100-0600", "", group = gSy, inline = "s")
syCol  = input.color(#7e57c2, "", group = gSy, inline = "s")

gBox = "=====  SESSION BLOCKS  ====="
showBox   = input.bool(true, "Show Range Blocks", group = gBox)
boxTrans  = input.int(85, "Block Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gBox)
boxBorder = input.bool(true, "Show Dashed Border", group = gBox)
showCandle= input.bool(false, "Show Session Candle", group = gBox, tooltip = "Draws the whole session as one candle: a body from its open to its close and a wick across its full range.")
candleW   = input.float(0.30, "Candle Body Width (share of session)", minval = 0.05, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gBox)

gLbl = "=====  SESSION LABELS  ====="
showLbl   = input.bool(true, "Show Labels", group = gLbl)
lblSize   = input.string("Small", "Label Size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = gLbl)
lblStagger= input.bool(true, "Stagger Overlapping Labels", group = gLbl, tooltip = "Offsets each market's labels vertically so overlapping sessions never collide.")
lblGap    = input.float(0.6, "Stagger Spacing (x ATR)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 5, step = 0.1, group = gLbl)
showPts   = input.bool(true, "Show Change In Points", group = gLbl, inline = "c")
showPct   = input.bool(true, "Show Change In Percent", group = gLbl, inline = "c")

gPan = "=====  SUMMARY PANEL  ====="
showPanel = input.bool(true, "Show Panel", group = gPan)
panPos    = input.string("Bottom Right", "Position", options = ["Top Left", "Top Center", "Top Right", "Middle Left", "Middle Center", "Middle Right", "Bottom Left", "Bottom Center", "Bottom Right"], group = gPan)
panOrder  = input.string("Left to Right", "Order", options = ["Left to Right", "Right to Left"], group = gPan)
panRows   = input.int(9, "Miniature Candle Height", minval = 3, maxval = 20, group = gPan, tooltip = "How many text rows tall the miniature candle in each panel column is drawn.")
panSize   = input.string("Small", "Panel Text Size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = gPan)
panTrans  = input.int(80, "Panel Column Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gPan)
showDot   = input.bool(true, "Show Open / Closed Status", group = gPan)

gSty = "=====  STYLE  ====="
colUp    = input.color(#26a69a, "Bullish Candle", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colDn    = input.color(#ef5350, "Bearish Candle", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colPanBg = input.color(#0b1020, "Panel Frame", group = gSty)

string szL = lblSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : lblSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.small
string szP = panSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : panSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.small

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  T I M E F R A M E   S U I T A B I L I T Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bool intraday = timeframe.isintraday or timeframe.isseconds
bool tfOk     = intraday

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S E S S I O N   S T A T E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
type SessState
    bool  active = false
    float o      = na
    float h      = na
    float l      = na
    float c      = na
    float vol    = 0.0
    int   sb     = 0
    box   bx     = na
    box   body   = na
    line  wk     = na
    label lb     = na
    bool  done   = false

var array<SessState> st = array.from(SessState.new(), SessState.new(), SessState.new(), SessState.new())

var array<box>   hBox  = array.new<box>()
var array<box>   hBody = array.new<box>()
var array<line>  hWick = array.new<line>()
var array<label> hLbl  = array.new<label>()

// session presence, evaluated individually so each session string stays a simple value
bool in0 = tkOn and tfOk and not na(time(timeframe.period, tkSess, tz))
bool in1 = ldOn and tfOk and not na(time(timeframe.period, ldSess, tz))
bool in2 = nyOn and tfOk and not na(time(timeframe.period, nySess, tz))
bool in3 = syOn and tfOk and not na(time(timeframe.period, sySess, tz))

array<bool>   inArr  = array.from(in0, in1, in2, in3)
array<bool>   onArr  = array.from(tkOn, ldOn, nyOn, syOn)
array<string> nmArr  = array.from("Tokyo", "London", "New York", "Sydney")
array<color>  clArr  = array.from(tkCol, ldCol, nyCol, syCol)

float atrRef = nz(ta.atr(14), math.max(high - low, syminfo.mintick * 10))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H E L P E R S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fmtVol(float v) =>
    string s = "n/a"
    if not na(v) and v > 0
        float a = math.abs(v)
        s := a >= 1e9 ? str.tostring(v / 1e9, "#.##") + "B" : a >= 1e6 ? str.tostring(v / 1e6, "#.##") + "M" : a >= 1e3 ? str.tostring(v / 1e3, "#.#") + "K" : str.tostring(v, "#.#")
    s

// change text, absolute and percentage, exactly as reported on the label and in the panel
changeTxt(float o, float c) =>
    string s = ""
    if not na(o) and not na(c) and o != 0
        float d = c - o
        float p = d / o * 100.0
        string sign = d >= 0 ? "" : "-"
        string a = sign + str.tostring(math.abs(d), format.mintick)
        string b = "(" + (d >= 0 ? "" : "-") + str.tostring(math.abs(p), "#.##") + "%)"
        s := showPts and showPct ? a + " " + b : showPts ? a : showPct ? b : ""
    s

// a session's whole price action drawn as a column of text, used inside the panel
miniCandle(float o, float h, float l, float c, int rows) =>
    string s = ""
    if na(o) or na(h) or na(l) or na(c)
        s := "-"
    else
        float rng = h - l
        if rng <= 0
            s := "-"
        else
            float bh = math.max(o, c)
            float bl = math.min(o, c)
            for r = 0 to rows - 1
                float hi = h - rng * r / rows
                float lo = h - rng * (r + 1) / rows
                bool isBody = bl <= hi and bh >= lo
                s := s + (isBody ? "█" : "│")
                if r < rows - 1
                    s := s + "\n"
    s

detailTip(string nm, float o, float h, float l, float c, float v) =>
    nm + "\n" + "Open   " + str.tostring(o, format.mintick) + "\n" + "High   " + str.tostring(h, format.mintick) + "\n" + "Low    " + str.tostring(l, format.mintick) + "\n" + "Close  " + str.tostring(c, format.mintick) + "\n" + "Range  " + str.tostring(h - l, format.mintick) + "\n" + "Volume " + fmtVol(v)

panelPosition() =>
    panPos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : panPos == "Top Center" ? position.top_center : panPos == "Top Right" ? position.top_right : panPos == "Middle Left" ? position.middle_left : panPos == "Middle Center" ? position.middle_center : panPos == "Middle Right" ? position.middle_right : panPos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : panPos == "Bottom Center" ? position.bottom_center : position.bottom_right

prune(array<box> a, int cap) =>
    while a.size() > cap
        box.delete(a.shift())

pruneL(array<line> a, int cap) =>
    while a.size() > cap
        line.delete(a.shift())

pruneB(array<label> a, int cap) =>
    while a.size() > cap
        label.delete(a.shift())

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  P E R - S E S S I O N   S T A T E   M A C H I N E
//  Each session opens, accumulates live, then locks when it closes. Historical sessions are final.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bool anyOpened = false
bool anyClosed = false

for i = 0 to 3
    SessState s = st.get(i)
    bool inS = inArr.get(i)
    color c   = clArr.get(i)

    if inS and not s.active
        // ---- session opens ----
        s.active := true
        s.done   := false
        s.o      := open
        s.h      := high
        s.l      := low
        s.c      := close
        s.vol    := nz(volume)
        s.sb     := bar_index
        anyOpened := true

        if showBox
            s.bx := box.new(bar_index, high, bar_index, low, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = boxBorder ? color.new(c, 25) : color.new(c, 100), border_width = 1, border_style = line.style_dashed, bgcolor = color.new(c, boxTrans))
            hBox.push(s.bx)
        if showCandle
            s.wk := line.new(bar_index, high, bar_index, low, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(c, 20), width = 1)
            s.body := box.new(bar_index, math.max(open, close), bar_index, math.min(open, close), xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(c, 10), border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(close >= open ? colUp : colDn, 45))
            hWick.push(s.wk)
            hBody.push(s.body)
        if showLbl
            s.lb := label.new(bar_index, high, "", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = c, size = szL)
            hLbl.push(s.lb)

    else if inS and s.active
        // ---- session running: accumulate live ----
        s.h   := math.max(nz(s.h, high), high)
        s.l   := math.min(nz(s.l, low), low)
        s.c   := close
        s.vol := nz(s.vol) + nz(volume)

    else if not inS and s.active
        // ---- session closes: values lock here ----
        s.active := false
        s.done   := true
        anyClosed := true

    // ---- redraw whatever this session currently owns ----
    if (s.active or s.done) and not na(s.o)
        int right = s.active ? bar_index : (na(s.bx) ? bar_index : box.get_right(s.bx))

        if not na(s.bx)
            box.set_lefttop(s.bx, s.sb, s.h)
            box.set_rightbottom(s.bx, right, s.l)
        if not na(s.wk)
            int mid = math.round((s.sb + right) / 2)
            line.set_xy1(s.wk, mid, s.h)
            line.set_xy2(s.wk, mid, s.l)
            int halfW = math.max(1, int(math.round((right - s.sb) * candleW / 2)))
            box.set_lefttop(s.body, mid - halfW, math.max(s.o, s.c))
            box.set_rightbottom(s.body, mid + halfW, math.min(s.o, s.c))
            box.set_bgcolor(s.body, color.new(s.c >= s.o ? colUp : colDn, 45))
            box.set_border_color(s.body, color.new(s.c >= s.o ? colUp : colDn, 10))
        if not na(s.lb)
            float stag = lblStagger ? atrRef * lblGap * (i + 1) : atrRef * 0.4
            label.set_xy(s.lb, math.round((s.sb + right) / 2), s.h + stag)
            label.set_text(s.lb, nmArr.get(i) + "\n" + str.tostring(s.c, format.mintick) + "\n" + changeTxt(s.o, s.c))
            label.set_tooltip(s.lb, detailTip(nmArr.get(i), s.o, s.h, s.l, s.c, s.vol))

int cap = math.max(4, maxHist * 4)
prune(hBox,  cap)
prune(hBody, cap)
pruneL(hWick, cap)
pruneB(hLbl, cap)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S U M M A R Y   P A N E L
//  One column per enabled session: status, name, price, change and a miniature candle rendered
//  from that session's own open, high, low and close.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table pan  = na
var table warn = na

if barstate.islast
    table.delete(pan)
    table.delete(warn)

    if not tfOk and tfGuard
        warn := table.new(position.middle_center, 1, 1, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60))
        table.cell(warn, 0, 0, "Market Sessions Overview Panel\n\nSessions divide the trading day, so this tool is meaningful on\nintraday timeframes only. Please switch to an intraday chart.", bgcolor = color.new(colPanBg, 5), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)

    else if showPanel
        // collect the enabled sessions in the requested order
        array<int> cols = array.new<int>()
        for i = 0 to 3
            if onArr.get(i)
                cols.push(i)
        if panOrder == "Right to Left" and cols.size() > 1
            array<int> rev = array.new<int>()
            for k = cols.size() - 1 to 0
                rev.push(cols.get(k))
            cols := rev

        int n = cols.size()
        if n > 0
            pan := table.new(panelPosition(), n, 5, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(colPanBg, 20), frame_width = 2, frame_color = color.new(colPanBg, 10))

            for k = 0 to n - 1
                int i = cols.get(k)
                SessState s = st.get(i)
                color c  = clArr.get(i)
                color bg = color.new(c, panTrans)
                string nm = nmArr.get(i)

                bool   live = s.active
                float  o = s.o
                float  h = s.h
                float  l = s.l
                float  cl = s.c
                float  v = s.vol
                float  chg = not na(o) and not na(cl) and o != 0 ? (cl - o) / o * 100.0 : na
                color  chgC = na(chg) ? color.new(color.gray, 30) : chg >= 0 ? colUp : colDn
                string tip = na(o) ? nm + "\nNo session data yet" : detailTip(nm, o, h, l, cl, v)

                table.cell(pan, k, 0, showDot ? (live ? "● OPEN" : "● CLOSED") : "", bgcolor = bg, text_color = live ? colUp : colDn, text_size = szP, tooltip = live ? nm + " is open" : nm + " is closed")
                table.cell(pan, k, 1, nm, bgcolor = bg, text_color = c, text_size = szP, tooltip = tip)
                table.cell(pan, k, 2, na(cl) ? "-" : str.tostring(cl, format.mintick), bgcolor = bg, text_color = c, text_size = szP, tooltip = tip)
                table.cell(pan, k, 3, na(chg) ? "-" : "(" + (chg >= 0 ? "" : "-") + str.tostring(math.abs(chg), "#.##") + "%)", bgcolor = bg, text_color = chgC, text_size = szP, tooltip = tip)
                table.cell(pan, k, 4, miniCandle(o, h, l, cl, panRows), bgcolor = bg, text_color = na(o) or na(cl) ? color.new(color.gray, 30) : cl >= o ? colUp : colDn, text_size = szP, tooltip = tip)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A L E R T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(in0 and not in0[1], "Sessions - Tokyo Open",    "Market Sessions Overview Panel: the Tokyo session opened on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(in1 and not in1[1], "Sessions - London Open",   "Market Sessions Overview Panel: the London session opened on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(in2 and not in2[1], "Sessions - New York Open", "Market Sessions Overview Panel: the New York session opened on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(in3 and not in3[1], "Sessions - Sydney Open",   "Market Sessions Overview Panel: the Sydney session opened on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(not in0 and in0[1], "Sessions - Tokyo Close",    "Market Sessions Overview Panel: the Tokyo session closed on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(not in1 and in1[1], "Sessions - London Close",   "Market Sessions Overview Panel: the London session closed on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(not in2 and in2[1], "Sessions - New York Close", "Market Sessions Overview Panel: the New York session closed on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(not in3 and in3[1], "Sessions - Sydney Close",   "Market Sessions Overview Panel: the Sydney session closed on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(in1 and in2 and not (in1[1] and in2[1]), "Sessions - London / New York Overlap Begins", "Market Sessions Overview Panel: the London and New York overlap has begun on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(anyOpened, "Sessions - Any Session Opened", "Market Sessions Overview Panel: a trading session has opened on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(anyClosed, "Sessions - Any Session Closed", "Market Sessions Overview Panel: a trading session has closed on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(in0 ? 1 : 0, "Tokyo Active",    color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(in1 ? 1 : 0, "London Active",   color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(in2 ? 1 : 0, "New York Active", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(in3 ? 1 : 0, "Sydney Active",   color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(in1 and in2 ? 1 : 0, "London / NY Overlap", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)